# GlobalSign Root CA (unsuffixed, the original ~1998 legacy root -- distinct
# from GlobalSign Root CA - R3/R6/R46/E46, which ARE in ESP-IDF's bundled
# cacrt_all.pem). Needed because our server_url (synora.carcise.dev, fronted
# by Cloudflare) serves a chain -- leaf -> Google Trust Services "WE1" ->
# "GTS Root R4" -- where GTS Root R4 is presented cross-signed BY this exact
# root, not in its own self-signed form. ESP-IDF's bundle is missing this
# root entirely (confirmed: absent from both cacrt_all.pem and
# cacrt_deprecated.pem), so esp-x509-crt-bundle can't close the chain and
# esp_crt_bundle_attach() fails with "No matching trusted root certificate
# found" even though the self-signed GTS Root R4 IS nominally in the bundle
# (ECDSA P-384 root-matching in esp-crt-bundle has known gaps for non-P-256
# curves, so that entry doesn't help here either). Sourced from this
# machine's own ca-certificates package (/etc/ssl/certs/GlobalSign_Root_CA.pem),
# not fetched fresh -- this is a long-published, stable, well-known root
# (SHA-256 fingerprint EB:D4:10:40:E4:BB:3E:C7:42:C9:E3:81:D3:1E:F2:A4:1A:48:
# B6:68:5C:96:E7:CE:F3:C1:DF:6C:D4:33:1C:99).
# See main/boards/common/device_activation.cc and sdkconfig.defaults
# (MBEDTLS_CUSTOM_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE) for how this gets merged in.
